WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.128
I’m addicted to internet personality tests.

00:00:03.128 --> 00:00:06.256
For instance, my inner Disney princess: Belle.

00:00:06.297 --> 00:00:12.303
I’m an ENFP on the Meyers Briggs, a 7 wing
6 on the Enneagram, and a Gryffindor, DUH.

00:00:12.303 --> 00:00:16.599
Those can be fun, but most of them don’t
have much practical use.

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:19.519
Such an Enneagram 1 thing to say...

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:23.940
However, psychologists and financial practitioners
around the globe have started to identify

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.359
a myriad of distinct MONEY personalities.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:31.865
Now, this isn’t an exact science, but rather
a lens that you can look through to better

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.616
understand your own money habits.

00:00:33.616 --> 00:00:38.955
The names vary slightly, but there are 6 main
types that seem to be emerging.

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:44.419
Uncovering your personal money sign might
just be the lodestar that can guide you to

00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:46.713
a more healthy relationship with your money.

00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:57.057
Do you love playing the stock market?

00:00:57.057 --> 00:01:00.685
Do you spend your free time researching cryptocurrency
and emerging tech?

00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:02.645
Are you a Motley Fool premium subscriber?

00:01:02.645 --> 00:01:06.900
If you feel called out then you might be a
RISK TAKER.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:11.279
The great thing about this type is their high
financial literacy and openness to talking

00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:12.447
about money.

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:14.365
However there are some hangups.

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:19.245
Greg Davies who headed a financial behavior
department at Barclays observes that hopping

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:23.666
from one opportunity to the next “fires
up the pleasure centers in the brain.

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:28.922
The longer you stay in an addictive environment,
the more prone you are to bad decisions, which

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:33.093
causes anxiety, which leads to overtrading
and therefore more anxiety.”

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:38.264
So if this is you, try your best to slim down
your financial media intake and consider having

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:43.103
a cooler financial head around you to bounce
ideas off of before you start learning how

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:47.565
to day-trade or invest in your mother’s
best friend’s “surefire” business idea.

00:01:47.565 --> 00:01:49.484
Next up, the HOARDER.

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:54.614
To Hoarders, money represents security against
the unknowns of the world.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.783
Building up savings comes easy to them.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.952
But there’s another side to that coin.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.328
Pun intended.

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:05.041
That golden number of ultimate security seems
always just out of reach.

00:02:05.041 --> 00:02:09.796
And the minute you bring a non-hoarder partner
into the mix, things can get ugly.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:14.134
Activities like vacationing and going to a
nice restaurant can seem threatening to their

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.135
stability.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:19.430
If this is you, you can ease the intensity
of those fears by having a having a cash-based

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.431
budget.

00:02:20.431 --> 00:02:24.310
That way you can always see where your true
savings lies and can feel more at ease

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:28.523
treating yourself and taking a calculated
risk now and then.

00:02:28.523 --> 00:02:31.109
Hello, I’m Julia and I’m a SOCIAL SPENDER.

00:02:31.109 --> 00:02:32.861
Hi, Julia.

00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:39.159
I love to shop simply for its own sake, but
usually not ever in large one time amounts...

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.994
just small things all over the place.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:45.623
I also love to buy things for friends and
family and give my money away to causes I’m

00:02:45.623 --> 00:02:47.041
passionate about.

00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:51.546
To me, buying and spending is the ultimate freedom of expression

00:02:51.546 --> 00:02:54.090
which can obviously backfire pretty spectacularly.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:03:00.013
And if I’m honest, I tend to carry around
some shame that my type is inherently wrong

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:02.390
and bound for financial ruin.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:07.812
Thankfully for me, I also found peace in...you
guessed it...a budget.

00:03:07.812 --> 00:03:12.525
Even though I was terrified that budgeting
would curb my fun, it ended up cutting the

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:15.695
shame strings that were attached to that spending!

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:22.577
Now, with a flexible plan, I can scratch my
shopping itch without sabotaging my future self

00:03:22.744 --> 00:03:27.373
Next we have those slayers of spreadsheets,
beancounters extraordinaire, the ENGINEERS;

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.334
a type I know well.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.668
To us, money is a game.

00:03:30.668 --> 00:03:36.925
A game meant to be won through savvy and constant
vigilance which can sometimes border on obsession.

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:41.846
We tend to be interested in investing but
are more anxious than our risk-taker cousins,

00:03:41.846 --> 00:03:44.515
likely to scuttle the ship at the first sign
of trouble.

00:03:44.515 --> 00:03:48.728
Claudia Hammond, a psychology lecturer notes
“people who find it hard to deal with the

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:52.106
unpredictability of life can get super organized
about money.”

00:03:52.106 --> 00:03:55.526
If you're like me, you might consider hiring a financial professional

00:03:55.526 --> 00:04:00.365
that can help you see the forest for the trees
and make sure you’re not over-complicating things.

00:04:00.531 --> 00:04:04.285
And if you’re partnered with a different
money type, a relationship counselor might

00:04:04.285 --> 00:04:05.703
not be the worst idea.

00:04:05.703 --> 00:04:10.833
We all have that friend that has to loudly
claim the check whenever they go out.

00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:16.047
They also probably have the latest smartphone,
a luxury car, and designer clothes.

00:04:16.047 --> 00:04:18.258
That’s the MOGUL.

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:24.180
Money for them is a tool meant for a very
specific purpose; to achieve higher social status.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.807
Forget keeping up with the Joneses.

00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:28.142
They ARE the Joneses.

00:04:28.142 --> 00:04:32.522
Interestingly enough, the social groups that
have the highest prevalence of this behaviour

00:04:32.522 --> 00:04:35.733
tend to have a history of systemic poverty.

00:04:35.733 --> 00:04:40.029
The hottest luxury markets in the world are
in countries with below average household

00:04:40.029 --> 00:04:46.286
income.These visible displays of wealth are
meant to psychologically combat the perception

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:47.537
of poverty.

00:04:47.537 --> 00:04:52.375
Social media only exacerbates this situation,
pressuring people to compete not just with

00:04:52.375 --> 00:04:54.585
their neighbors, but the whole world.

00:04:54.585 --> 00:04:59.215
So moguls seeking to be a healthier version
of themselves might consider limiting their

00:04:59.215 --> 00:05:00.591
social media interactions.

00:05:00.591 --> 00:05:05.221
Don’t let your flex gram of today leave
you scrounging for change in your later years.

00:05:05.221 --> 00:05:09.058
If I asked you how much you spend in a month,
could you tell me?

00:05:09.058 --> 00:05:12.437
What about how much you make or what’s in
your accounts right now?

00:05:12.437 --> 00:05:18.026
If you’re breaking out in hives just thinking
about it, then you may be our last type:

00:05:18.026 --> 00:05:19.027
The OSTRICH.

00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:22.905
Honestly, congrats for being here and watching
a financial video!

00:05:22.905 --> 00:05:28.953
Because for you, talking about money brings
up all sorts of bad feelings like fear, anxiety

00:05:28.953 --> 00:05:30.038
and disgust.

00:05:30.038 --> 00:05:31.748
This could be for many reasons.

00:05:31.748 --> 00:05:36.627
You might have a lot of shame about your current
situation or have experienced financial trauma

00:05:36.627 --> 00:05:37.837
in your past.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:42.467
You may be able to avoid confronting your
money fears for a time, but we all know that

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:45.053
creates bigger problems down the road.

00:05:45.053 --> 00:05:49.307
Money avoidance has even been associated with
increased risk of overspending and compulsive

00:05:49.307 --> 00:05:50.308
buying.

00:05:50.308 --> 00:05:53.603
You’ll have to get your head out of the
sand, but you probably won’t be able to

00:05:53.603 --> 00:05:54.604
do it alone.

00:05:54.604 --> 00:05:57.899
Find someone who can hold your hand and help
you work through things like your spending

00:05:57.899 --> 00:05:59.317
habits or your debt picture.

00:05:59.317 --> 00:06:05.948
I promise, 90% of the time the situation isn’t
nearly as bad as ostriches imagine it to be.

00:06:05.948 --> 00:06:08.993
Darkness often acts like a steroid to your
fears.

00:06:08.993 --> 00:06:13.122
So, take a deep breath and text your most
supportive friend.

00:06:13.122 --> 00:06:14.123
You got this!

00:06:14.123 --> 00:06:17.960
While you may resonate more strongly with
one or two of these types, it’s important

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.880
to remember we’re all ultimately a mix.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.840
We contain multitudes.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:27.804
Your personal money style is formed by your
family history, worldview, and experiences,

00:06:27.804 --> 00:06:29.889
and it’s neither good nor bad.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:34.394
The goal of identifying your sign is not to
change it, but hopefully empower you to become

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:36.562
become a healthier version of your type.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:42.318
And in our personal and professional experience,
taking the time to get to know yourself better

00:06:42.318 --> 00:06:45.279
is one of the best investments you can make!

00:06:45.279 --> 00:06:46.906
And that’s our two cents!

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:51.160
Thanks to our patrons for keeping Two Cents financially healthy!

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.920
Click the link in the description to become a Two Cents patron!

